  range: 163.9% to 456.4% of the observed displacement
  [OK] the induced displacement is 164-456% of DESI's, reported as computed

====================================================================================================
S5. VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  WHAT IS SETTLED HERE. The sign question for channel C is answered by an actual fit rather
  than a template argument, on a mock with a realistic redshift distribution and a
  marginalised absolute magnitude. The amplitude is ample (S1: MI-amplified steps exceed
  the phantom signal band), so amplitude was never the obstacle.

  WHAT THE FRAMEWORK ACTUALLY CONTRIBUTES, stated narrowly. The monopole is NOT an MI
  prediction -- the local void is an observational claim (KBC / local hole) with its own
  contested status. MI supplies only the amplification factor nu ~ 1.2-1.7 on whatever
  contrast exists. So even in the best case this framework is a MULTIPLIER on someone
  else's mechanism, not the mechanism. Novelty is correspondingly thin, exactly as the
  audit warned: the local-void and timescape literatures own the effect, and 'the DESI hint
  is biased by low-z supernovae' is already published without any modified inertia.

  WHAT WOULD KILL IT (and should be checked before anyone invests):
   1. Modern compilations DO apply peculiar-velocity and local-flow corrections. The
      relevant residual is the part their LCDM-calibrated reconstruction MISSES, i.e.
      roughly (nu - 1) x the modelled flow, not the full flow. That is a 20-70% correction,
      not a 100% one, and it shrinks every number in S2-S4 accordingly.
   2. The KBC void's depth and extent are contested; a shallower or more distant edge
      weakens the step.
   3. The DESI contours are a NARROW anticorrelated ellipse. Reproducing the amplitude is
      not enough -- a candidate bias must reproduce the DEGENERACY DIRECTION too, which is
      the tighter constraint and the one S3 tests.
   4. BAO is independent of SN calibration and also prefers evolving DE at 3.1 sigma with
      NO supernovae at all. A purely SN-side artifact cannot explain that component, so at
      best this channel accounts for the SN contribution, not the whole signal.
      *** THIS IS THE HARDEST OBJECTION AND IT IS STRUCTURAL, NOT COSMETIC. ***
====================================================================================================
